#!/usr/bin/env python3
#
# ops — the weekly Operations meeting: the FigJam board shows it, Azure DevOps holds the
# tiltak. One command per moment of the week:
#
#   ops neste [dato] [--dry]   before the meeting: clone the right template as «Referat <dato>»,
#                              fill its tiltakslogg with the open tiltak, create the meeting epic
#   ops add ["<tekst>"]        any time: the line goes in a queue and ops returns at once; a worker
#                              in the background has Haiku sort it into a tema, makes a tiltak an
#                              ADO Issue, and puts either kind on the board as a sticky (tiltak in
#                              the tema's Utfall, notat in its Rapport). «t: …» / «n: …» force the
#                              kind. Without text: type one innspill after another, the queue shows
#   ops kø [--igjen]           the queue and how far each innspill has come; --igjen retries errors
#   ops watch [--en] [--dry]   while the meeting runs: watches the next meeting's page, and an Utfall
#                              sticky without #id that has stopped changing becomes an ADO Issue; the
#   (o, åpne, sync)            sticky is rewritten as «#id tittel / Ansvarlig / Frist», with a small
#                              … mark in its corner while ops works on it, gone when it's done. Opens
#                              the page first. --en: one pass, nothing opened
#   ops log                    the open tiltak by due date: x = løst, u = +1 uke
#   ops lukk [dato] [--dry]    after the meeting: Utfall stickies without #id become Issues, the
#                              rest becomes the referat in the epic, and the meeting is closed
#
# neste, log and lukk also tidy up: an epic whose meeting is over and whose Issues are all
# Done is closed.
#
# Each tema on a referat page holds a Rapport and an Utfall section. A sticky with «#1234»
# is tiltak 1234 in ADO; lukk skips those, log turns them green when they're done.
# The meeting epic «Operations-møte <dato>» is closed for writing once lukk has written its
# referat (LUKKET marker); add then targets the next meeting, and its stickies wait in the
# queue until `ops neste` has made that page.
#
# Reading the board needs a Figma personal access token (file_content:read), in
# FIGMA_TOKEN or the keychain:
#   security add-generic-password -a "$USER" -s figma-token -w '<figd_…>' -U
# Writing goes through the Figma MCP server (`claude -p`), which needs a one-time
# `/mcp` → figma → Authenticate in an interactive claude session.
#
# OPS_FIGMA_FILE overrides the board, OPS_MODEL the sorting model (haiku),
# OPS_REFERAT_MODEL the model that writes the referat (sonnet).

